Subject: [EXPERIMENT] drm/msm: A14 port-one RGB8 DSC8 at 4K60

Baseline: linux-msm/laptops-kernel 51231839d5ef007638bd1c3500e6a76b337a66f3
plus the A14 postPatch transformations captured in a14-dsc-baseline.tar.gz.
Apply AFTER those transformations. Not an upstream-ready patch.

Adapted from JS Deck's fac6d5b9dfb715a2d849365f62ddc9b8310992bf:
https://gist.github.com/xzn/028a18f78f6fa6f08a8a0d6a3d29c232
Based on Kuogee Hsieh's Qualcomm DP DSC series:
https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/1674498274-6010-1-git-send-email-quic_khsieh@quicinc.com/
Original copyright and license notices are retained in source files.

This adaptation preserves the captured uncompressed TU algorithm, removes
unrelated candidate CRTC/CWB/command-mode changes, checks sink DSC/FEC
capabilities, uses actual slice count, initializes encoder counts, and keeps
DP DTO parameters separate from DPU private parameter population.

The boot-only msm.a14_dp_dsc_test parameter defaults OFF. The companion
NixOS test module enables it. It is limited to UX3407NA af54000 DP, two
lanes at HBR2/HBR3, and exactly 3840x2160/533250 kHz RGB8 with DSC8.
The candidate is compile-tested, not tested on A14 hardware.

